@host = http://localhost:5218

### The default account is the pickup directory, so this needs no server: it writes ./mail-drop/*.eml.
POST {{host}}/welcome?name=John

### A named account. "capture" is the in-memory transport, which keeps the message instead of sending.
POST {{host}}/welcome?name=Ada&account=capture

### Reads back what the in-memory transport kept. Empty until the request above has run.
GET {{host}}/captured

### A non-ASCII name, to see RFC 2047 encoding in the written .eml rather than mojibake.
POST {{host}}/welcome?name=Zo%C3%AB%20%E4%BD%A0%E5%A5%BD

### Refused before a message is built: %0D%0A decodes to CRLF, and EmailAddress.TryParse will not
### make a display name out of it. MimeKit would have stripped it and delivered a mangled header.
POST {{host}}/welcome?name=John%0D%0ABcc:%20attacker@evil.com

### AccountNotFound, retryable false: nothing declares an account by this name. Startup validation
### cannot catch this one, because a name may always come from an IMailAccountSource at send time.
POST {{host}}/welcome?name=Ada&account=nope

### A real server. Uncomment the "live" account in appsettings.json first and supply the password as
### Mailer__Accounts__live__Settings__Password in the environment. Without it the account resolves
### and the send fails with InvalidAccount, naming the missing setting.
POST {{host}}/welcome?name=John&account=live
